---
const steps = [
  { id: 'discover', title: 'Discover a capability', label: 'Discover', tech: 'The Graph', body: 'Start with the capability a task needs. Network queries indexed registration information to find candidate providers.', note: 'Discovery supplies candidates; it does not authorize a service call.' },
  { id: 'verify', title: 'Verify the service identity', label: 'Verify identity', tech: 'ENS / ERC-8004 / Agent Card', body: 'Cross-check the readable name, registered agent and public Agent Card. The identity, HTTPS execution address and supported protocol must agree.', note: 'Invalid records or a mismatched endpoint stop the request before calling or paying.' },
  { id: 'quote', title: 'Get a quote. Check the budget.', label: 'Quote & budget', tech: 'x402 payment requirements', body: 'Get the price for this request and compare it with the consumer’s allowed budget. Paid access is scoped to the individual call.', note: 'A quote outside the budget never proceeds to execution.' },
  { id: 'payment', title: 'Verify the payment conditions', label: 'Verify payment', tech: 'x402 / Blocky402', body: 'The client supplies a signed payment payload. Network asks the payment facilitator to verify it before granting access to the capability.', note: 'Verification confirms the payment conditions. Final settlement follows successful execution.' },
  { id: 'execute', title: 'Put the capability to work', label: 'Execute', tech: 'A2A / Frely / Frely Swarm', body: 'Frely receives the authorized A2A request and passes the task to Swarm. Swarm runs the corresponding Skill, Agent or workflow in its execution environment.', note: 'Prompts, agent code and the runtime stay off-chain.' },
  { id: 'settle', title: 'Settle and return the result', label: 'Settle & return', tech: 'Hedera / x402', body: 'After successful execution, the facilitator settles the quoted payment on Hedera. The consumer receives the result with the associated settlement evidence.', note: 'One execution ID links the request, its retries, the result and the payment record.' },
];
---

<section id="flow" class="story-section capability-flow" aria-labelledby="flow-heading" data-testid="capability-flow">
  <div class="flow-layout">
    <div class="flow-navigation">
      <h2 id="flow-heading" class="story-heading" data-reveal>From discovery<br /><span>to a paid result.</span></h2>
      <p class="story-intro" data-reveal>An agent can find, verify and purchase the capability it needs, one request at a time.</p>
      <nav class="flow-options" aria-label="Capability purchase walkthrough"><ol class="flow-index">
        {steps.map((step, index) => <li><a href={`#flow-${step.id}`} data-flow-link={step.id} aria-current={index === 0 ? 'step' : undefined}><span class="flow-option-number">0{index + 1}</span>{step.label}<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" /></svg></a></li>)}
      </ol></nav>
      <p class="flow-caption">How the network works</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-card-viewport">
    <ol class="flow-stages" aria-label="Capability purchase steps">
      {steps.map((step, index) => (
        <li id={`flow-${step.id}`} class="flow-stage" data-flow-stage={step.id} data-testid={`flow-step-${step.id}`}>
          <div class="flow-stage-top"><span class="flow-stage-number">0{index + 1}</span><span class="flow-tech">{step.tech}</span></div>
          <h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.body}</p>
          <div class="flow-note"><span aria-hidden="true"></span><p>{step.note}</p></div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-principles" data-reveal>
    <div><h3>Verify before proceeding.</h3><p>Discovery failures, invalid addresses and inconsistent identities end the flow before any service call or payment.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Keep every retry accountable.</h3><p>Retries share an execution ID. An uncertain payment is checked before proceeding, preventing a timeout from becoming a second charge.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import "../scripts/flow-wheel";
</script>
